55,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option A is easiest for the treasurer, but Option B seems fairer for the members.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A guarantees our fixed costs are covered, which is my main priority for stability.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Option C sounds like the named-grade years, which I found out caused friction. I dislike it.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,May,,Option B makes people hesitate to come. I think Option A is better for the social vibe.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option B is the only one that stops the ""ghosts"" from being subsidized by the regulars.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, but the treasurer's hours would be insane with Option B. I can't support that.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, I agree. The administrative burden of Option B is a hidden cost we can't afford.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@May, if we go with Option A, how do we handle the people who can't pay upfront?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,May,,"@Minako, we can just be flexible with them privately, as long as the structure is simple.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, stability is fine, but fairness is better. Option B is the most rational choice.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Minato,,I'm leaning towards Option A. It's the only way to keep the books manageable.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for Option A. It's the only way to ensure the account doesn't run dry.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Minako,,I'll go with Option A. It avoids the friction of tiers and the barrier of per-event fees.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,May,,Option A for me. Let's make it easy for people to just show up.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,You're all choosing convenience over equity. I'm sticking with Option B.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
